            <ArticleTitle>Endophthalmitis after pars plana vitrectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>815-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In three cases of bacterial endophthalmitis following pars plana vitrectomy the important diagnostic findings included increased orbital pain, decreased visual acuity, and the presence of a hypopyon. Despite agressive antibiotic therapy, all three eyes became blind, and two progressed rapidly to phthisis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
